<title>USA: Pennsylvania Gov challenges court's bible tax.</title>
<headline>Pennsylvania Gov challenges court's bible tax.</headline>
<dateline>HARRISBURG, Pa. 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Gov. Tom Ridge said he would challenge a court ruling making the bible and other religious publications subject to state sales tax.</p>
<p>The Commonwealth Court declared the exemption unconstitutional last week, and the Ridge Administration filed an appeal with the state Supreme Court.</p>
<p>Stores have been told to continue to exempt the affected books from sales tax until the appeal is completed.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
